# --- tgkb app-data dir (AD-8 / NFR-1) ---
# Config, encrypted Telegram session + api_hash, and the SQLite database
# (with WAL/SHM sidecars) all live under one gitignored, host-local dir.
# NEVER commit any of these — they hold secrets and local state.
.tgkb-data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*-wal
*-shm
*.session
*.session-journal

# --- local secrets (Story 1.3 manual testing) ---
# .env holds real Telegram creds (TG_API_ID / TG_API_HASH / TG_PHONE) for local
# `tgkb auth` runs. NEVER commit it — api_hash is a secret (NFR-1). The tracked
# .env.example is the safe placeholder template; the real .env stays local only.
.env
!.env.example

# --- Python ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- uv ---
# uv.lock IS committed (pins the full transitive tree) — do not ignore it.

# --- Local dev tooling & BMAD artifacts (not part of the project) ---
# Personal Claude Code / BMAD tooling and planning output. These are local
# workflow scaffolding, not part of the shipped package — keep them out of the
# public repo.
.claude/
_bmad/
_bmad-output/
.pytest_cache/

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
